 types and the distribution of total_vaccinations_per_hundred values.\n```\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import stats\n\n# Load the data\ndf = pd.read_csv(\'./input/country_vaccinations.csv\')\n\n# Display basic info\nprint("Dataset shape:", df.shape)\nprint("\\nColumn names:", df.columns.tolist())\nprint("\\nData types:")\nprint(df.dtypes)\n```\n```markdown\nNow I\'ll check the unique vaccine types and filter for the ones specified in the question.\n```\n```python\n# Check unique vaccines\nprint("Unique vaccines in dataset:")\nprint(df[\'vaccines\'].unique())\n\n# Filter for specified vaccines\nspecified_vaccines = [\'Pfizer/BioNTech\', \'Moderna\', \'Oxford/AstraZeneca\', \'Johnson&Johnson/Janssen\']\ndf_filtered = df[df[\'vaccines\'].isin(specified_vaccines)].copy()\n\nprint("\\nNumber of rows after filtering vaccines:", len(df_filtered))\nprint("Vaccines in filtered data:", df_filtered[\'vaccines\'].unique())\n```\n```markdown\nNow I need to filter out rows with null values in total_vaccinations_per_hundred column.\n```\n```python\n# Filter out rows with null values in total_vaccinations_per_hundred\ndf_clean = df_filtered[df_filtered[\'total_vaccinations_per_hundred\'].notna()].copy()\n\nprint("Number of rows after removing null values:", len(df_clean))\nprint("\\nNull values in total_vaccinations_per_hundred:", df_clean[\'total_vaccinations_per_hundred\'].isna().sum())\n```\n```markdown\n[STEP GOAL]: Perform One-Way ANOVA test to check for significant differences in total_vaccinations_per_hundred between vaccine groups.\n```\n```markdown\nI\'ll now perform the One-Way ANOVA test. First, I need to group the data by vaccine type and extract the total_vaccinations_per_hundred values for each group.\n```\n```python\n# Group by vaccine and extract total_vaccinations_per_hundred\nvaccine_groups = df_clean.groupby(\'vaccines\')[\'total_vaccinations_per_hundred\'].apply(list)\n\nprint("Sample sizes per vaccine group:")\nfor vaccine, values in vaccine_groups.items():\n    print(f"{vaccine}: {len(values)} samples")\n\n# Prepare data for ANOVA\ngroups = [vaccine_groups[vaccine] for vaccine in vaccine_groups.index]\n```\n```markdown\nNow I\'ll perform the One-Way ANOVA test using scipy.stats.f_oneway.\n```\n```python\n# Perform One-Way ANOVA\nf_statistic, p_value = stats.f_oneway(*groups)\n\nprint(f"\\nF-statistic: {f_statistic}")\nprint(f"P-value: {p_value}")\nprint(f"P-value rounded to 4 decimal places: {round(p_value, 4)}")\n\n# Determine significance\nsignificance = "yes" if p_value < 0.05 else "no"\nprint(f"Significant difference: {significance}")\n```\n```markdown\n[STEP GOAL]: Create the FinalAnswerBlock with the required output format.\n```\n```markdown\nI\'ll now create the final answer block with the required format.\n```\n```python\n# Create the final answer block\nfinal_answer = {\n    "final_answer_block": {\n        "question_id": 124,\n        "answers": {\n            "significance_of_difference": significance,\n            "p_value": round(p_value, 4)\n        },\n        "format_targets": {\n            "significance_of_difference": f"@significance_of_difference[{significance}]",\n            "p_value": f"@p_value[{round(p_value, 4)}]"\n        },\n        "evidence": {\n            "source_columns": ["country", "total_vaccinations_per_hundred", "vaccines"],\n            "sample_size": len(df_clean),\n            "method": "One-Way ANOVA test on total_vaccinations_per_hundred grouped by vaccine type",\n            "oracle_evidence": {\n                "feature_columns": ["vaccines"],\n                "target": "total_vaccinations_per_hundred",\n                "split": "N/A (no train/test split for ANOVA)",\n                "random_state": "N/A",\n                "metric": "F-statistic and p-value from scipy.stats.f_oneway"\n            }\n        },\n        "verified": True,\n        "validator_report_id": None\n    }\n}\n\nprint("Final Answer Block:")\nimport json\nprint(json.du