n2. Filter for countries using Pfizer/BioNTech, Moderna, Oxford/AstraZeneca, and Johnson&Johnson/Janssen\n3. Remove rows with null values in total_vaccinations_per_hundred\n4. Extract the relevant columns for ANOVA analysis\n```\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import stats\n\n# Load the data\ndf = pd.read_csv(\'./input/country_vaccinations.csv\')\n\n# Display basic info\nprint(f"Original shape: {df.shape}")\nprint(f"Columns: {df.columns.tolist()}")\nprint(f"\\nVaccine types in dataset:")\nprint(df[\'vaccines\'].value_counts())\n```\n```markdown\nNow I need to filter the data according to the requirements:\n1. Only keep the 4 specified vaccines\n2. Remove rows with null values in total_vaccinations_per_hundred\n3. Prepare data for ANOVA\n```\n```python\n# Define the vaccines to consider\ntarget_vaccines = [\'Pfizer/BioNTech\', \'Moderna\', \'Oxford/AstraZeneca\', \'Johnson&Johnson/Janssen\']\n\n# Filter for target vaccines\ndf_filtered = df[df[\'vaccines\'].isin(target_vaccines)].copy()\n\n# Remove rows with null values in total_vaccinations_per_hundred\ndf_clean = df_filtered.dropna(subset=[\'total_vaccinations_per_hundred\'])\n\nprint(f"Shape after filtering: {df_clean.shape}")\nprint(f"\\nVaccine distribution after filtering:")\nprint(df_clean[\'vaccines\'].value_counts())\nprint(f"\\nMissing values in total_vaccinations_per_hundred: {df_clean[\'total_vaccinations_per_hundred\'].isnull().sum()}")\n```\n```markdown\nNow I need to prepare the data for One-Way ANOVA. I\'ll group by vaccine type and extract the total_vaccinations_per_hundred values for each group.\n```\n```python\n# Group by vaccine and extract the values for ANOVA\nvaccine_groups = df_clean.groupby(\'vaccines\')[\'total_vaccinations_per_hundred\'].apply(list)\n\n# Display sample data for each group\nprint("Sample data per vaccine group:")\nfor vaccine, values in vaccine_groups.items():\n    print(f"\\n{vaccine}:")\n    print(f"  Count: {len(values)}")\n    print(f"  Mean: {np.mean(values):.4f}")\n    print(f"  Std: {np.std(values, ddof=1):.4f}")\n    print(f"  Min: {min(values):.4f}")\n    print(f"  Max: {max(values):.4f}")\n```\n```markdown\nNow I\'ll perform the One-Way ANOVA test to check if there\'s a significant difference between the vaccine groups.\n```\n```python\n# Prepare data for ANOVA - extract lists of values for each vaccine group\ngroups = [group[\'total_vaccinations_per_hundred\'].tolist() \n          for name, group in df_clean.groupby(\'vaccines\')]\n\n# Perform One-Way ANOVA\nf_statistic, p_value = stats.f_oneway(*groups)\n\nprint(f"ANOVA Results:")\nprint(f"F-statistic: {f_statistic:.4f}")\nprint(f"P-value: {p_value:.4f}")\nprint(f"\\nSignificant (p < 0.05): {p_value < 0.05}")\n```\n```markdown\n[STEP GOAL]: Verify the ANOVA results and prepare the final output in the required format.\n```\n```markdown\nI need to:\n1. Verify the p-value is between 0 and 1\n2. Round the p-value to 4 decimal places\n3. Determine significance based on p-value < 0.05\n4. Format the output correctly\n```\n```python\n# Round p-value to 4 decimal places\np_value_rounded = round(p_value, 4)\n\n# Determine significance\nsignificance = "yes" if p_value_rounded < 0.05 else "no"\n\nprint(f"Final Results:")\nprint(f"Significance: {significance}")\nprint(f"P-value: {p_value_rounded}")\n\n# Verify p-value is in valid range\nassert 0 <= p_value_rounded <= 1, "P-value must be between 0 and 1"\n```\n```markdown\n[STEP GOAL]: Create the FinalAnswerBlock with the required format.\n```\n```markdown\nI need to create the final answer block with:\n- question_id: 124\n- answers: significance_of_difference and p_value\n- format_targets: @significance_of_difference[significance] and @p_value[p_value]\n- evidence: source_columns, sample_size, method, oracle_evidence\n```\n```markdown\n{\n  "final_answer_block": {\n    "question_id": 124,\n    "answers": {\n      "significance_of_difference": "yes",\n      "p_value": 0.0\n    },\n    "format_targets": {\